1
00:00:03,340 --> 00:00:04,240
Down here!

2
00:00:04,480 --> 00:00:06,377
My Harmon will hit you all the harder!

3
00:00:06,460 --> 00:00:07,290
Underwater...

4
00:00:07,373 --> 00:00:09,577
turquoise blue...

5
00:00:09,660 --> 00:00:11,040
OVERDRIVE!

6
00:00:17,700 --> 00:00:18,977
He did it! Bravo!

7
00:00:19,060 --> 00:00:20,380
That was amazing!

8
00:00:20,800 --> 00:00:21,980
It's not over yet!

9
00:00:23,160 --> 00:00:26,337
I can't believe Bluford was able
to dodge that blast of Harmon.

10
00:00:26,420 --> 00:00:27,857
He moved so fast underwater.

11
00:00:27,940 --> 00:00:29,420
He was all a blur.

12
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:32,647
My overdrive barely
clansed off his forehead.

13
00:00:33,680 --> 00:00:36,357
Now I know anything
less than a solid punch

14
00:00:36,440 --> 00:00:39,087
won't be enough to send
the Hormone into him.

15
00:00:39,240 --> 00:00:42,900
My good Lord Dio, I thank
thee for this life anew,

16
00:00:43,100 --> 00:00:45,417
that I may duel with
this stout-hearted lad.

17
00:00:45,500 --> 00:00:48,437
My heart would swell to
bursting if it still beats.

18
00:00:48,520 --> 00:00:51,220
In blood and deed, he
is the stuff of heroes.

19
00:00:51,900 --> 00:00:54,620
Now we will fight in our native element.

20
00:00:55,060 --> 00:00:59,900
It is by mastery of our arts and strength
of our spirits that we wage this duel.

21
00:01:00,700 --> 00:01:01,880
Bear your soul.

22
00:01:02,020 --> 00:01:05,432
Hold nothing back lest you not
survive beyond this moment.

23
00:01:08,120 --> 00:01:11,940
Even as Dio's puppet, his pride
is a force to be reckoned with.

24
00:01:12,160 --> 00:01:16,037
But his knightly valor has been
twisted into a wanton love of violence.

25
00:01:16,120 --> 00:01:19,061
When I best you, I'll take
your head as my trophy.

26
00:01:19,200 --> 00:01:20,997
It's easy to let your hair do the work.

27
00:01:21,080 --> 00:01:24,200
Come, withstand my hormone
face to face like a man.

28
00:01:36,360 --> 00:01:37,800
Let's go.

29
00:01:59,880 --> 00:02:04,017
I'm going to build a way
of the power of the earth.

30
00:02:04,100 --> 00:02:08,717
If you are finding the way of
the world, the path of the world!

31
00:02:08,800 --> 00:02:12,617
I'm going to be a boy.

32
00:02:12,700 --> 00:02:13,697
I'm going to live with the land.

33
00:02:13,780 --> 00:02:14,610
I'm going

34
00:02:14,693 --> 00:02:20,797
to live with

35
00:02:20,880 --> 00:02:21,710
the path of the world.

36
00:02:21,793 --> 00:02:26,780
I'm going to live with
the heart of the world.

37
00:03:01,740 --> 00:03:02,780
Overtry Barrage!

38
00:03:11,700 --> 00:03:12,530
Jojo!

39
00:03:20,000 --> 00:03:21,540
This is terrible.

40
00:03:22,180 --> 00:03:24,897
Harmon can only be projected
through the arms and the legs.

41
00:03:24,980 --> 00:03:27,357
With his arms bound in
front of him like that,

42
00:03:27,440 --> 00:03:30,977
he has no way of blasting through
that infernal hair of Bluford's.

43
00:03:31,060 --> 00:03:31,890
I...

44
00:03:31,973 --> 00:03:35,422
I want to help him out, but you
and me have got things even worse.

45
00:03:35,540 --> 00:03:38,140
I think old Tarkus fancies a dust-up.

46
00:03:41,620 --> 00:03:45,840
His hair, it's tearing through
my clothes, through my skin.

47
00:03:46,160 --> 00:03:50,513
The more I struggle, the tighter it
winds, and it's sucking my blood away.

48
00:03:55,840 --> 00:03:59,500
Beat your petty life adieu,
behold the coup de grace!

49
00:04:00,180 --> 00:04:04,004
I'll take your head and bathe in
a fountain of life-giving blood!

50
00:04:04,840 --> 00:04:05,960
Take this!

51
00:04:12,940 --> 00:04:17,380
Watts is not all that conducts
hormones, Metal Silver Overdrive!

52
00:04:20,000 --> 00:04:21,200
What a brain!

53
00:04:21,400 --> 00:04:26,106
Using his sword to hoist Bluford by his
own bleeding petard, Who thinks of that?

54
00:04:28,600 --> 00:04:30,560
How my heart resonates.

55
00:04:31,020 --> 00:04:33,440
I'm pulsing with heat and life.

56
00:04:35,600 --> 00:04:38,680
My very blood is a symphony within me.

57
00:04:39,300 --> 00:04:42,800
Sunlight, yellow, overdrive!

58
00:04:45,460 --> 00:04:47,220
There we go, that's it.

59
00:04:47,420 --> 00:04:50,361
About time we heard the
welcome crackle of Harmon.

60
00:04:52,900 --> 00:04:56,417
When I pummeled Bluford a moment
ago, something felt different.

61
00:04:56,500 --> 00:05:00,029
Knowing his past makes his
present corruption all the worse.

62
00:05:00,320 --> 00:05:01,320
Take heart, Jojo.

63
00:05:01,480 --> 00:05:03,060
He is that man no longer.

64
00:05:03,500 --> 00:05:06,800
He's nothing but a zombie,
eager to spread his evil.

65
00:05:07,540 --> 00:05:09,420
You must be the one to end him.

66
00:05:13,720 --> 00:05:15,940
Boy, I'm the Black Knight, Bluford.

67
00:05:16,720 --> 00:05:18,160
Strike me as thou wilt.

68
00:05:18,340 --> 00:05:19,580
This pain is nothing.

69
00:05:21,080 --> 00:05:22,637
He's still dangerous, mate!

70
00:05:22,720 --> 00:05:23,550
Look out!

71
00:05:25,140 --> 00:05:27,917
He's been missing an arm
and scorched all the hell.

72
00:05:28,000 --> 00:05:30,765
He's laying into Jojo
every bit as ferociously.

73
00:05:34,700 --> 00:05:35,530
What the?

74
00:05:35,613 --> 00:05:36,933
Don't just stand there!

75
00:05:37,060 --> 00:05:37,890
Do something!

76
00:05:38,040 --> 00:05:41,393
If you don't get out of there
now, it's curtains for you!

77
00:05:46,720 --> 00:05:48,400
Have they both gone mad?

78
00:05:49,860 --> 00:05:51,331
What are they doing, huh?

79
00:05:52,620 --> 00:05:54,040
A moment to go.

80
00:05:54,300 --> 00:05:56,240
You said this pain is nothing.

81
00:05:57,000 --> 00:06:00,580
That means pain is something
you can feel again.

82
00:06:02,460 --> 00:06:04,560
Oh, the flowers.

83
00:06:05,020 --> 00:06:06,940
They're blooming all around him.

84
00:06:07,460 --> 00:06:12,520
Even now, the hormone ravages the evil
that animates Bluford's long-dead corpse.

85
00:06:16,780 --> 00:06:22,537
You see the long forgotten pain came
back only humans know that sort of ache.

86
00:06:22,620 --> 00:06:26,177
Observe my dear Speed
Wagon his zombie body

87
00:06:26,260 --> 00:06:29,157
succumbs to the hormone but his noble soul

88
00:06:29,240 --> 00:06:32,237
is redeemed in the
process I could sense the

89
00:06:32,320 --> 00:06:34,908
good in you that's why
I didn't try to dodge

90
00:06:35,600 --> 00:06:40,937
You could have killed me just now but
you stayed your hand look at his face

91
00:06:41,020 --> 00:06:44,937
it's like all the rage and hatred he
had when Dio brought him back are gone.

92
00:06:45,020 --> 00:06:49,726
His features are so gentle he could be a
bloke catching up with his oldest mate.

93
00:06:50,580 --> 00:06:54,697
You stood there like a statue,
ready to take the fatal blow.

94
00:06:54,780 --> 00:06:56,540
Oblivion beckoned, but you

95
00:06:57,060 --> 00:06:58,217
put your trust in me.

96
00:06:58,300 --> 00:07:00,900
Your faith in human goodness is rare.

97
00:07:05,360 --> 00:07:07,897
One side have railed
against the pain I feel.

98
00:07:07,980 --> 00:07:10,820
Now, going to my rightful
end, I cherish all

99
00:07:12,880 --> 00:07:13,917
that proves me human.

100
00:07:14,000 --> 00:07:15,497
It gives me joy.

101
00:07:15,580 --> 00:07:18,857
The embers dull within
me, but I am tranquil.

102
00:07:18,940 --> 00:07:19,770
There

103
00:07:20,180 --> 00:07:21,757
is no bitterness left.

104
00:07:21,840 --> 00:07:26,880
What irony to live yet again,
dying with thanks on my lips for

105
00:07:30,260 --> 00:07:32,378
the very man who slaughters me anew.

106
00:07:32,580 --> 00:07:35,237
I shall return to my one true master.

107
00:07:35,320 --> 00:07:38,537
I would know The name of
the warrior who bested me

108
00:07:38,620 --> 00:07:43,840
would you kindly do me that
honor it's jonathan joestar?

109
00:07:45,200 --> 00:07:48,937
Sir Jonathan I leave you
this sword given to me

110
00:07:49,020 --> 00:07:52,040
by my precious queen and
the word engraved upon it

111
00:07:53,540 --> 00:07:56,917
Luck but first let me affix my

112
00:07:57,000 --> 00:08:02,300
own benediction pluck sir bluefoot

113
00:08:10,400 --> 00:08:12,020
Go you to your rest.

114
00:08:12,260 --> 00:08:14,907
Let no one doubt you
have earned it, Bluford.

115
00:08:15,740 --> 00:08:16,570
Why?

116
00:08:16,960 --> 00:08:20,078
Why did I have to strike
him down to redeem his soul?

117
00:08:20,800 --> 00:08:25,400
He died once before with hate in his
heart, but his spirit was still pure.

118
00:08:25,760 --> 00:08:30,180
He returned not out of choice,
but dragged above by Dio's evil.

119
00:08:30,520 --> 00:08:32,580
His evil in the mosque's power.

120
00:08:32,880 --> 00:08:35,586
I will send them both
to hell before the dawn.

121
00:08:36,380 --> 00:08:37,210
Jojo!

122
00:08:37,293 --> 00:08:38,394
He's right behind you!

123
00:08:39,060 --> 00:08:39,890
Tarkus!

124
00:08:43,380 --> 00:08:44,520
You villain!

125
00:08:44,840 --> 00:08:47,957
That was the armor of a
steadfast friend and comrade!

126
00:08:48,040 --> 00:08:49,900
He died with honor and dignity!

127
00:08:50,280 --> 00:08:52,360
He died like a spineless dog!

128
00:08:52,820 --> 00:08:56,780
He was too clever by half, liked
winning his fights with thinking.

129
00:08:57,140 --> 00:08:59,800
I just hit him until they fall to pieces!

130
00:09:00,760 --> 00:09:02,620
What use have I got for clever?

131
00:09:02,940 --> 00:09:05,297
I carry a sword as tall as a man!

132
00:09:05,380 --> 00:09:08,020
None of you will get an easy death.

133
00:09:22,880 --> 00:09:24,660
Jojo, nice catch.

134
00:09:26,260 --> 00:09:27,920
The cliff is crumbling.

135
00:09:31,060 --> 00:09:34,720
These dead leaves. Jojo. Yes, sir.

136
00:09:39,240 --> 00:09:42,220
My magnetism, overdrive!

137
00:09:51,160 --> 00:09:52,260
Hurry, Poco!

138
00:09:52,600 --> 00:09:54,260
Speedwagon, grab on!

139
00:10:01,340 --> 00:10:04,377
All human beings, whether
adept at Hamon or not,

140
00:10:04,460 --> 00:10:07,080
constantly exude a weak magnetic field.

141
00:10:07,520 --> 00:10:10,461
An overdrive can increase
the power of that field.

142
00:10:11,100 --> 00:10:15,982
Jojo and Zeppeli sent it into the leaves,
drawing them together into a solid sheet.

143
00:10:17,500 --> 00:10:18,540
Wow! Bye!

144
00:10:22,940 --> 00:10:23,900
We're flying!

145
00:10:24,180 --> 00:10:25,298
I can't believe it!

146
00:10:25,480 --> 00:10:27,127
I bet you're magicians, huh?

147
00:10:27,360 --> 00:10:28,557
You'd have to be, right?

148
00:10:28,640 --> 00:10:31,917
How did you learn to do all of these
neat spells in the first place?

149
00:10:32,000 --> 00:10:33,057
Damn good question!

150
00:10:33,140 --> 00:10:36,375
I've been watching them do
it and I still pinch myself.

151
00:10:36,520 --> 00:10:38,400
Oi, Baron, what's the story?

152
00:10:38,600 --> 00:10:40,071
We're not going anywhere.

153
00:10:40,240 --> 00:10:43,181
How on earth did you pick
up all this mumbo-jumbo?

154
00:10:52,480 --> 00:10:57,560
Many years ago, my travels took me to
India, where I discovered a mysterious man.

155
00:10:58,200 --> 00:10:59,960
He called himself a doctor,

156
00:11:00,240 --> 00:11:03,717
though he was very young and
lacked all the tools of the trade.

157
00:11:03,800 --> 00:11:07,897
Little did I know, he was more potent
of a medic than I'd ever encountered.

158
00:11:07,980 --> 00:11:12,451
He took a gangrenous limb in his hands
and healed it with light from within.

159
00:11:12,920 --> 00:11:15,220
That was the day I learned of Hamon.

160
00:11:16,000 --> 00:11:19,557
I'd been looking for something with
which to fight the stone mask's evil,

161
00:11:19,640 --> 00:11:21,520
and in Hamon, I had found it.

162
00:11:22,500 --> 00:11:23,382
Eager to learn,

163
00:11:23,500 --> 00:11:25,977
I crossed into Tibet
and up the Salween River

164
00:11:26,060 --> 00:11:29,080
in search of he who had
taught the young healer.

165
00:11:35,380 --> 00:11:38,020
His name was Tonpetty.

166
00:11:51,660 --> 00:11:55,700
Stranger, these eyes of
mine have seen your future.

167
00:11:56,300 --> 00:12:02,020
If you pursue the mysteries of Harmon
as my pupil, your fate is sealed.

168
00:12:02,820 --> 00:12:06,080
The day will come when this
will be the death of you.

169
00:12:06,860 --> 00:12:08,080
I understand.

170
00:12:09,140 --> 00:12:12,980
If I must die to end this quest, so be it.

171
00:12:21,680 --> 00:12:25,997
Master Tonpedi's prophecy is never far
from my mind, but I cannot tell them.

172
00:12:26,080 --> 00:12:27,280
Not even Jojo.

173
00:12:28,040 --> 00:12:28,870
Baron?

174
00:12:31,420 --> 00:12:32,740
So, that sound?

175
00:12:33,160 --> 00:12:35,748
That's part of Halmon
doing its thing, yeah?

176
00:12:36,320 --> 00:12:37,150
Hardly.

177
00:12:37,320 --> 00:12:38,980
Look out, it's Tarkus!

178
00:12:49,180 --> 00:12:53,440
He's insane, leaping from that height
just to give chase to his foes.

179
00:12:56,680 --> 00:13:00,337
There's a goodly amount of Hormone
holding these leaves together, you brute.

180
00:13:00,420 --> 00:13:02,538
Painful to the touch for the United.

181
00:13:03,200 --> 00:13:04,030
What's that?

182
00:13:04,220 --> 00:13:07,117
That's where the Knights used
to train in the olden days.

183
00:13:07,200 --> 00:13:08,397
Lead to safety, everyone.

184
00:13:08,480 --> 00:13:10,656
Before we get swatted out of the sky.

185
00:13:17,540 --> 00:13:20,957
Crazy Blighter, he just slammed
himself straight into the tower!

186
00:13:21,040 --> 00:13:24,457
Yes, and thank your lucky
stars that he did Speedwagon.

187
00:13:24,540 --> 00:13:27,997
Unlike their master Dio's
minions can't regenerate

188
00:13:28,080 --> 00:13:30,904
so that should be the
last we see of that beast?

189
00:13:37,200 --> 00:13:38,030
How did...

190
00:13:38,113 --> 00:13:39,413
he should be mincemeat?

191
00:13:39,560 --> 00:13:41,740
Even in death, he has a will of iron.

192
00:13:42,100 --> 00:13:44,865
How does his body endure
under such punishment?

193
00:13:45,000 --> 00:13:46,280
He's climbing up!

194
00:13:46,660 --> 00:13:50,020
We can't destroy Dio while
this monster dogs our steps.

195
00:13:50,260 --> 00:13:52,201
It seems we have no other choice.

196
00:13:52,460 --> 00:13:54,578
Tarkus meets his doom here and now.

197
00:13:55,600 --> 00:13:57,400
Jojo, this will be perilous.

198
00:13:57,620 --> 00:13:59,326
Get the lad to safety within.

199
00:14:13,000 --> 00:14:13,960
This door.

200
00:14:14,400 --> 00:14:15,871
Something's odd about it.

201
00:14:16,180 --> 00:14:17,140
Be careful.

202
00:14:17,420 --> 00:14:20,157
This is where they used to train
the knights how to kill people.

203
00:14:20,240 --> 00:14:22,240
They say it's full of booby traps.

204
00:14:24,020 --> 00:14:25,080
Doc Jojo!

205
00:14:25,300 --> 00:14:26,829
Something's coming at you!

206
00:14:30,500 --> 00:14:31,330
Jojo!

207
00:14:35,140 --> 00:14:36,500
Who ensnared me?

208
00:14:39,800 --> 00:14:40,630
Sorokas!

209
00:14:41,560 --> 00:14:43,060
Yes, caught you good.

210
00:14:43,440 --> 00:14:45,380
Your fleet of foot, little man.

211
00:14:45,600 --> 00:14:48,247
But now you and me are
chained to each other.

212
00:14:48,380 --> 00:14:49,909
You've got nowhere to run.

213
00:14:52,980 --> 00:14:56,057
Jojo had wandered into the
lair of the Two-Headed Dragon,

214
00:14:56,140 --> 00:14:59,669
an ancient sparring ground and
home of the Chain Deathmatch.

215
00:15:00,060 --> 00:15:02,060
I killed 48 men here.

216
00:15:02,280 --> 00:15:05,320
Taking a life's an art
form, and I'm a master.

217
00:15:08,900 --> 00:15:09,730
That's enough.

218
00:15:10,040 --> 00:15:11,277
You can't punch through it.

219
00:15:11,360 --> 00:15:12,772
That door is solid iron.

220
00:15:13,560 --> 00:15:16,678
Goodness, he's batted his
knuckles bloody against it.

221
00:15:17,320 --> 00:15:18,791
Harmon is very versatile,

222
00:15:19,000 --> 00:15:22,397
but it's meant to be used as a
rapier, not as a sledgehammer.

223
00:15:22,480 --> 00:15:26,068
Bricks I could beat to a powder,
but this door is too strong.

224
00:15:26,360 --> 00:15:27,837
Jojo faces a darker dilemma.

225
00:15:27,920 --> 00:15:31,802
That chain about his neck is more
than ripple energy can overcome.

226
00:15:32,400 --> 00:15:36,797
Breaking out of that collar is impossible,
and you'll need the key to unlock it.

227
00:15:36,880 --> 00:15:38,292
Too bad it's right here.

228
00:15:40,140 --> 00:15:44,277
During a deathmatch, the door to the
outside is fashioned to lock tight.

229
00:15:44,360 --> 00:15:48,713
Just as I have the key to your collar,
you have the one that goes to mine.

230
00:15:49,080 --> 00:15:53,139
Therefore, the only way that either
of us is going to get out of here

231
00:15:54,460 --> 00:15:56,580
is by taking the other's head!

232
00:15:57,920 --> 00:15:58,750
Come on!

233
00:16:00,060 --> 00:16:00,890
Overdrive!

234
00:16:10,040 --> 00:16:12,037
The chain is touching the stone ceiling,

235
00:16:12,120 --> 00:16:15,002
so the Hormone lacks a
direct path into Taruchus.

236
00:16:21,780 --> 00:16:24,160
He's broken the bone in my forearm.

237
00:16:25,740 --> 00:16:26,897
It's a simple thing to fix.

238
00:16:26,980 --> 00:16:29,156
A little Hormone and I'm good as new.

239
00:16:29,300 --> 00:16:33,500
But in order to use Hormone, I need
to be free of this damnable collar.

240
00:16:33,860 --> 00:16:35,140
I can't breathe.

241
00:16:39,320 --> 00:16:40,150
Jojo!

242
00:16:41,100 --> 00:16:43,597
Oh no, this is all so frightening.

243
00:16:43,680 --> 00:16:44,960
I think I wet myself.

244
00:16:45,500 --> 00:16:48,620
This village was safe
until these men arrived.

245
00:16:48,960 --> 00:16:50,078
I'm in danger here.

246
00:16:50,320 --> 00:16:53,817
You need to get away from all this
fighting with the double Pogo.

247
00:16:53,900 --> 00:16:55,677
I see a lever, Baron Zeppeli.

248
00:16:55,760 --> 00:16:59,517
No telling for certain, but I think
pulling on it will open this door.

249
00:16:59,600 --> 00:17:02,257
Fighting Tarkus is a daunting
enough task as it is,

250
00:17:02,340 --> 00:17:05,634
never mind doing it fresh out
of a battle with Blueford.

251
00:17:06,140 --> 00:17:07,477
Come, hella high water.

252
00:17:07,560 --> 00:17:10,384
We must find a way to get
in there and help him.

253
00:17:11,240 --> 00:17:13,475
It's locked up tighter than a nunnery.

254
00:17:18,860 --> 00:17:19,960
It's so narrow.

255
00:17:20,880 --> 00:17:23,939
Try as they might, they
could never squeeze through.

256
00:17:25,040 --> 00:17:25,870
But...

257
00:17:27,660 --> 00:17:28,940
Maybe I could.

258
00:17:33,040 --> 00:17:33,870
Blast it!

259
00:17:34,000 --> 00:17:36,937
We could batter this door
till Judgment Day to no avail!

260
00:17:37,020 --> 00:17:39,957
We'll have to use the
cliffside entrance Tarkus used!

261
00:17:40,040 --> 00:17:41,864
But that'll take too much time!

262
00:17:42,000 --> 00:17:43,257
Time that he don't got!

263
00:17:43,340 --> 00:17:45,340
I know, but we've no other choice!

264
00:17:48,040 --> 00:17:50,400
Always on the bleeding sidelines!

265
00:17:51,900 --> 00:17:54,724
I'm powerless, there's
nothing I can do to help.

266
00:17:55,400 --> 00:17:57,557
Look at me, brat, I'm talking to you!

267
00:17:57,640 --> 00:18:01,240
I said look at me, are you stupid or what?

268
00:18:01,480 --> 00:18:03,197
He's such a little scary cat.

269
00:18:03,280 --> 00:18:05,657
What a baby, he's shaking like a leaf!

270
00:18:05,740 --> 00:18:07,237
Look, fellas, look at him.

271
00:18:07,320 --> 00:18:08,967
Oh is the baby going to cry?

272
00:18:17,920 --> 00:18:19,000
Hey, look.

273
00:18:22,380 --> 00:18:24,204
Come on, let's get out of here!

274
00:18:28,100 --> 00:18:29,577
Sis, it's you?

275
00:18:29,660 --> 00:18:31,280
Poco, really?

276
00:18:31,600 --> 00:18:34,071
You're letting those boys bully you again?

277
00:18:34,540 --> 00:18:38,680
They do this all the time Why not
try standing up to them for once?

278
00:18:39,400 --> 00:18:40,977
I'll bloody their noses!

279
00:18:41,060 --> 00:18:44,500
I will When? Tomorrow? In a year?

280
00:18:45,220 --> 00:18:46,280
I don't know

281
00:18:50,060 --> 00:18:52,942
Poco, what frightens you
more than anything else?

282
00:18:57,540 --> 00:19:00,257
I know that hurt, but
you're still in one piece.

283
00:19:00,340 --> 00:19:01,928
Pain's not the worst thing.

284
00:19:03,880 --> 00:19:05,760
There's something far worse.

285
00:19:07,100 --> 00:19:09,924
It's growing up being too
afraid to do anything.

286
00:19:10,380 --> 00:19:12,380
What kind of a life would that be?

287
00:19:15,060 --> 00:19:16,520
I'm sorry, sis.

288
00:19:20,960 --> 00:19:22,217
It's all right, Poco.

289
00:19:22,300 --> 00:19:24,829
Let's get you home into
some clean clothes.

290
00:19:37,060 --> 00:19:37,890
Poco!

291
00:19:38,520 --> 00:19:39,400
A window!

292
00:19:40,160 --> 00:19:41,000
Oi, lad!

293
00:19:41,440 --> 00:19:44,837
That's brave, but going in
there's gonna be the end of ya!

294
00:19:44,920 --> 00:19:46,626
Speedwagon, get the boy down!

295
00:19:46,760 --> 00:19:49,077
A butcher like Tarkus
doesn't care who he kills!

296
00:19:49,160 --> 00:19:51,395
He'll crush Pogo underfoot like a bug!

297
00:19:51,600 --> 00:19:52,440
Come on now!

298
00:19:52,640 --> 00:19:54,405
Enough of this nonsense, Pogo!

299
00:19:58,560 --> 00:20:02,717
Just think of what's gonna happen to
Winnight's Lot if these monsters win.

300
00:20:02,800 --> 00:20:06,940
If that Jojo guy gets killed in
here, they'll attack us next.

301
00:20:07,520 --> 00:20:08,920
What if they hurt Sis?

302
00:20:11,480 --> 00:20:14,500
I have to keep her safe, no matter what.

303
00:20:16,860 --> 00:20:17,690
Paces!

304
00:20:18,260 --> 00:20:20,160
I'm standing up to them now!

305
00:20:21,120 --> 00:20:22,220
Stay back!

306
00:20:22,460 --> 00:20:23,342
He'll kill you!

307
00:20:24,920 --> 00:20:27,220
Do not interfere, you brat!

308
00:20:33,660 --> 00:20:34,490
Poco!

309
00:20:36,080 --> 00:20:41,280
It hurt a lot, but I'm still
in one piece, so it's fine.

310
00:20:53,300 --> 00:20:55,580
I was brave, huh?

311
00:20:59,160 --> 00:21:01,380
Brave as a bear, my lad.

312
00:21:02,280 --> 00:21:03,110
Take heart.

313
00:21:03,300 --> 00:21:05,006
It's nothing that won't heal.

314
00:21:05,800 --> 00:21:07,300
Get him, Baron, go!

315
00:21:07,680 --> 00:21:09,980
Give that hulking bastard the what for!

316
00:21:21,200 --> 00:21:22,030
Zeppeli?

317
00:21:22,540 --> 00:21:27,140
The day will come when this
will be the death of you.

318
00:21:27,680 --> 00:21:32,680
In fine, is tonight the
night that I go to my grave.

319
00:21:34,720 --> 00:21:38,460
Fate is a fickle mistress,
but I cannot deny her.

320
00:21:40,260 --> 00:21:41,090
Zeppeli!

321
00:21:41,173 --> 00:21:43,400
Why do you sound so dire?

322
00:22:02,020 --> 00:22:05,117
I'll be the roundabout.

323
00:22:05,200 --> 00:22:09,277
The words will make you out and out.

324
00:22:09,360 --> 00:22:13,060
I'll spend the day your way.

325
00:22:14,600 --> 00:22:17,357
Call it morning driving through the sun.

326
00:22:17,440 --> 00:22:19,020
And in and out the valley.

327
00:22:28,900 --> 00:22:32,137
The music dance and sing.

328
00:22:32,220 --> 00:22:36,317
They make the children really ring.

329
00:22:36,400 --> 00:22:40,100
I spend the day your way.

330
00:22:41,560 --> 00:22:44,497
Cold in morning driving through the sun.

331
00:22:44,580 --> 00:22:46,320
And in and out the valley.

332
00:22:48,140 --> 00:22:50,940
And around the lake.

333
00:22:51,940 --> 00:22:54,337
Mountains come out of the sky.

334
00:22:54,420 --> 00:22:55,940
And they stand there.

335
00:22:59,300 --> 00:23:02,840
One mile over, we'll be
there and we'll see you.

336
00:23:05,680 --> 00:23:09,260
Ten and two summers, we'll be
there and I'll be with you.

337
00:23:12,720 --> 00:23:15,077
Twenty, four, five mile
over, we'll see you.

338
00:23:15,160 --> 00:23:17,940
I'll be there with you.

339
00:23:28,900 --> 00:23:31,520
This bloody savagery is unbelievable!

340
00:23:33,040 --> 00:23:34,340
Oh no! Tarkus!

341
00:23:34,440 --> 00:23:37,560
Pathetic waste of flesh! Jojo! Take it!

342
00:23:37,940 --> 00:23:39,300
Make it yours!
